 "documents": {
  "attachments": [
   {
    "name": "ambulance_agreement.txt",
    "text": "EVENT MEDICAL SERVICES AGREEMENT\nAgreement no. AG-92382\n\nBetween: Sentinel Ambulance Service (\"the Provider\")\nAnd: Greenhill Primary PTA (\"the Client\")\n\nEvent: Greenhill Summer Run Half Marathon\nEvent date: March 14, 2027\nLocation: Cathedral Green, Port Halden\n\nThe Provider will station one fully equipped ambulance with a crew of two paramedics on site at the top of Chapel Row from 07:00 until the last runner has finished or 12:30, whichever is later. The vehicle stays on site throughout and is dedicated to the event, except when transporting a patient from it.\n\nFee: $650, paid in full on signature.\n\nSigned for the Provider: Rhys Morgan, Operations Manager, January 8, 2027\nSigned for the Client: Helen Achterberg, January 8, 2027\n"
   },
   {
    "name": "crowd_plan.txt",
    "text": "Looking after people on the day: Greenhill Summer Run Half Marathon, Sunday 14 March 2027\n\nHelen Achterberg, Event Secretary, Greenhill Primary PTA\n\nFamilies are welcome, and there is usually a friendly atmosphere at the finish. Local shops have been supportive, and some stay open for the day. The prize-giving takes place at the end, and there is often a queue for tea.\n\nWe expect about 900 people altogether, including 620 runners. We allow for 280 spectators.\n\nWhere people will watch\nWe've set out three viewing spots with barriers: at the finish by the Civic Plaza, at the turn by Brook Street, and at the start by the top of Chapel Row. We measured them, and at about two people to the square metre they take around 1200 between them, which is more than we expect to come.\n\nHow we start the race\nWe set off in 3 waves, four minutes apart, with runners sorted by the time they expect to run. That thins everyone out before the first corner. The pens close five minutes before each wave goes.\n\nWho's helping\nWe've got 18 stewards in tabards, about one for every 50 people, with 2 supervisors in charge of sections. Each has a set position on a rota, and all come to a briefing an hour before the start.\n\nGetting everyone away\nRunners walk through a one-way funnel after the line, out to the recovery area, and leave by the north gate. Spectators have two marked ways out, and a steward stands at each to keep it clear. We reckon the whole place empties in 25 minutes.\n\nWho's in charge\nHelen Achterberg runs the event from the control point with a radio to every supervisor. They can hold a wave, stop the race, or make an announcement over the speakers to move people along. Supervisors call it in if a pen or viewing spot looks to be getting too full.\n"
   },
   {
    "name": "insurance.txt",
    "text": "Atlas Casualty Group\nCertificate of Insurance\n\nWe certify that a policy of event public liability insurance has been issued as follows.\n\nPolicy: EL-710833\nInsured: Greenhill Primary PTA\nEvent covered: Greenhill Summer Run Half Marathon\nLocation of event: Cathedral Green\nCover starts: 1 January 2027\nCover ends: 31 December 2027\nLimit of indemnity: $1,000,000 any one event\n\nSigned on behalf of the insurer, 8 January 2027\nCertificate reference AG-19330\n"
   },
   {
    "name": "medical_plan.txt",
    "text": "Medical cover for the Greenhill Summer Run Half Marathon, Sunday 14 March 2027\n\nFrom Helen Achterberg, Event Secretary, Greenhill Primary PTA\n\nThe race is a half marathon with 620 runners and starts at 08:30. On-site ambulance cover is set out in the attached paperwork from Sentinel Ambulance Service.\n\nFirst aid\nWe'll have 3 first aid posts, at the start, the finish and halfway, with 8 trained first aiders between them, so nobody on the course is more than about a kilometre and a half from help. We also have two first aiders on bikes, carrying defibrillators.\n\nHeat, cold and water\nThere's water every 2.5 km. We look at the forecast two days before and again two hours before. Over 28 degrees we start earlier or cut the course, and over 32 degrees we call it off. If it's cold or wet, we have foil blankets and a warm tent at the finish.\n\nIf someone needs hospital\nThe nearest emergency department is at Northshore District Hospital, 14 km from the finish. We've walked the route out from the pick-up point at the top of Chapel Row with the first aiders, and we've told the hospital the date and how many are coming.\n\nStaying in touch\nEveryone at a post and both bike first aiders has a radio on our medical channel, with phones as backup. Calls for an ambulance go through our medical lead, who tells the crew which barrier to come to.\n\nRunners get an email in race week telling them to dress for the weather and to keep a phone with them if they can. Most have run with us before. The list of entrants includes an emergency contact for each runner, which is kept at the start.\n\nWho's responsible\nOur medical lead is Fatima Haddad, a registered paramedic, who'll be there from an hour before the start until the last runner is in and has the final word on pulling any runner out.\n"
   },
   {
    "name": "police_letter.txt",
    "text": "PHPS TRAFFIC DIVISION - EVENT ATTENDANCE NOTICE\n\nTo: Greenhill Primary PTA (attn Helen Achterberg)\nFrom: Sgt. Karen Holt\nIssued: January 8, 2027\nOur ref: AG-97191\n\nEvent: Greenhill Summer Run Half Marathon\nDate of attendance: March 14, 2027\nLocation: Cathedral Green, starting at Chapel Row\n\nAttendance is confirmed. Escort: 2 motorcycles, 1 traffic car. On station from 07:00. Stand-down when the last runner clears the course.\n\nChanges to date or route must be notified to this office, because this notice applies only to the date and route shown.\n"
   },
   {
    "name": "race_plan.txt",
    "text": "Greenhill Summer Run Half Marathon: how the race will work\n\nPrepared by Helen Achterberg (Event Secretary), Greenhill Primary PTA. Last updated 8 January 2027.\n\nThis is our plan for race day, Sunday 14 March 2027. We expect 620 runners over half marathon (21 km). Numbers can be collected from the top of Chapel Row from an hour before we go at 08:30, and we aim to have the last finisher home by 12:00.\n\nThe route takes in Chapel Row, Harbour Boulevard, Brook Street and Lamb Street, and the City would need to close all of these for us. On the way round we cross Station Road, Church Road and Canal Road. We finish in the Civic Plaza.\n\nThere's plenty of room. Chapel Row is about 16 metres across, Brook Street about 16 metres and Lamb Street about 12 metres, and all have broad pavements too. We line up across the full width of Chapel Row, and the finish opens out into the Civic Plaza, where there's space for everyone.\n\nOur club has put on races for some years now and we keep to the same simple format: chip timing, water on the course, and a hot drink at the end. Results go up on our website the same evening.\n"
   },
   {
    "name": "traffic_plan.txt",
    "text": "Greenhill Summer Run Half Marathon - traffic notes\nSunday 14 March 2027 / gun 08:30 / Cathedral Green\ncontact Helen Achterberg 555-0120\nSee the attached correspondence from the police for the escort.\n\nCLOSURES\nSignal Hill Traffic Services doing barriers\nChapel Row (Salter Way-Abbey Road) 07:00-12:30\nHarbour Boulevard (Hatter Street-Abbey Road) 07:00-12:30\nBrook Street (Bridge Row-Copper Row) 07:00-12:30\nLamb Street (Orchard Road-Salter Way) 07:00-12:30\n\nMAJOR X-INGS\nall staffed from 07:00 til last runner\nStation Road x Harbour Boulevard: 2 marshals w/ boards + sup\nChurch Road x Lamb Street: 4 marshals w/ boards + sup\nCanal Road x Harbour Boulevard: 4 marshals w/ boards + sup\n\nDIVERSIONS\nsigned by Signal Hill Traffic Services\nChapel Row: via Queen's Road + Ferry Road, signs from Copper Row\nHarbour Boulevard: via Queen's Road + Regent Road, signs from Salter Way\nBrook Street: via Victoria Road + High Street, signs from Hatter Street\nLamb Street: via Cross Avenue + Victoria Road, signs from Abbey Road\n\nEMERGENCY\n3.5m lane kept clear whole way. radio at every barrier, open in 2 mins. controller has police + ambulance control direct\n\nNOTICE\nletter drop all frontages -21 days, reminder -7. boards up -10. bus co told\n\nREOPEN\nreopen when done and barriers picked up\n"
   }
  ],
  "cover_letter": "Hello,\n\nI am writing on behalf of our organisation about this year's race.\n\nHere is our application for the Greenhill Summer Run Half Marathon, Sunday 14 March 2027. 620 runners, half marathon, off at 08:30, around Cathedral Green. I've attached ambulance_agreement.txt, crowd_plan.txt, insurance.txt, medical_plan.txt, police_letter.txt, race_plan.txt, traffic_plan.txt.\n\nWe look forward to hearing from you.\n\nThanks,\nHelen\n\nHelen Achterberg, Greenhill Primary PTA\n555-0120\n",
